Plug-in name: users
Plug-in shortname: users
Description: function callees

Most options of the form '-users-option-name' and without any parameter
have an opposite with the name '-users-no-option-name'.

Most options of the form '-option-name' and without any parameter
have an opposite with the name '-no-option-name'.

Options taking a string as argument should preferably be written
-option-name="argument".

***** LIST OF AVAILABLE OPTIONS:

-users              compute function callees (opposite option is -no-users)

*** GETTING INFORMATION

-users-help         help of plug-in users
-users-h            alias for option -users-help

*** OUTPUT MESSAGES

-users-debug <n>    level of debug for plug-in users (default to 0)
-users-log <K_1:file_1,...>  copy log messages from users to a file. <K> is a
                    combination of these characters:
                    a: ALL messages (equivalent to 'dfiruw')
                    d: debug       e: user or internal error (same as 'iu')
                    f: feedback    i: internal error
                    r: result      u: user error    w: warning
                    An empty <K> (e.g. ":file.txt") defaults to 'iruw'. One
                    plug-in can output to several files and vice-versa.
                    (preferably use -users-log="K_1:file_1,...")
-users-msg-key <k1[,...,kn]>  enables message display for categories
                    <k1>,...,<kn>. Use -users-msg-key help to get a list of
                    available categories, and * to enable all categories
                    (preferably use -users-msg-key="k1[,...,kn]")
-users-verbose <n>  level of verbosity for plug-in users (default to 1)
-users-warn-key <k1[=s1][,...,kn[=sn]]>  set warning status for category <k1>
                    to <s1>,...,<kn> to <sn>. Use -users-warn-key help to get
                    a list of available categories, and * to enable all
                    categories. Possible statuses are inactive, feedback,
                    warning, error, abort, feedback-once, warning-once,
                    error-once. Defaults to warning. (preferably use
                    -users-warn-key="k1[=s1][,...,kn[=sn]]")
